      "writtenOn": "2020-11-09T09:55:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This could make use of iterators to make it look less crusty (C in Rust). I gives it a more function approach to state and avoids the need for on of the intermediate Vecs. I don\u0027t think you can avoid the final collect() unless you can check the tree hashes from the root to the leaf. Iterator would look something like:\n\n    const RANGE_OF_HASH_PAGE: u64 \u003d HASHES_PER_PAGE * PAGE_SIZE_U64;\n    const HASHES_PER_PAGE: u64 \u003d PAGE_SIZE_U64 / HASH_SIZE_U64;\n    \n    fn level_offsets(data_size: u64) -\u003e impl Iterator\u003cItem\u003du64\u003e {\n        if data_size \u003d\u003d 0 {\n            // TODO: what happens in this case? trailing_zeros() gives the bit width\n            //       for 0 so needs to be handled but what does fs-verity do?\n        }\n        let hash_pages \u003d divide_roundup(data_size, RANGE_OF_HASH_PAGE);\n        // TODO: fix casting and build time assert log_128 (HASHES_PER_PAGE\u003d128) is right\n        let max_level \u003d divide_roundup(hash_pages.trailing_zeros() as u64, 7) as u32;\n        (0..\u003dmax_level)\n            .rev()\n            .map(move |level| {\n                let level_range \u003d RANGE_OF_HASH_PAGE * HASHES_PER_PAGE.pow(level);\n                let level_hash_pages \u003d divide_roundup(data_size, level_range);\n                let level_size \u003d level_hash_pages * PAGE_SIZE_U64;\n                level_size\n            })\n            .scan(0, |sum, size| {\n                let offset \u003d *sum;\n                *sum \u003d *sum + size;\n                Some(offset)\n            })\n    }",
      "revId": "57fdfdfe6fb4a3baeba1f244a7d687852f34390e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
